            <ArticleTitle>Ehlers-Danlos hypermobility type in an adult with chronic pain and fatigue: a case study.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1248-1251</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.1046</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ehlers-Danlos syndrome hypermobility type (EDS-HT) is an underdiagnosed genetic connective tissue disorder that causes joint hypermobility and widespread pain. We present a patient with the chief complaint of shoulder pain, a long history of widespread joint pain, and associated comorbidities. EDS-HT provided a unifying diagnosis and direction for management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
